From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daryl Denson <9751141+denson9874@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 101/102] grizzly: preinstall the KernelSU Next manager with
 its native libs

ExpressiveOS ships KernelSU Next in init_boot; the manager is where the
user grants root, installs modules and turns on susfs. The module lives in
vendor/extra/ksu: Android.mk files aren't allowed under device/google/,
and Soong's android_app_import can't install an app's JNI libs. That
module installs the APK untouched (the kernel only trusts its upstream v2
signature) and its arm64 libs in /product/app/KernelSUNext/lib/arm64,
because Android never unpacks native libs for a system app it hasn't
updated. config.fs makes libksud.so executable: the manager runs it as a
program. Same as cheetah's and husky's.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Csz3tZY7m4dy7t6hausAkK
---
 BoardConfig.mk | 3 +++
 device.mk      | 7 +++++++
 ksu/config.fs  | 9 +++++++++
 3 files changed, 19 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 ksu/config.fs

diff --git a/BoardConfig.mk b/BoardConfig.mk
index 216498e..d646324 100644
--- a/BoardConfig.mk
+++ b/BoardConfig.mk
@@ -241,3 +241,6 @@ include $(IMAGES_PATH)/BoardConfigImages.mk
 # priv-apps lose their AOT code after every update and run interpreted/JIT
 # until background dexopt catches up (~180 MB, well inside super).
 BOARD_USES_SYSTEM_OTHER_ODEX :=
+
+# KernelSU Next manager (ExpressiveOS only): libksud.so is a program
+TARGET_FS_CONFIG_GEN += device/google/grizzly/ksu/config.fs
diff --git a/device.mk b/device.mk
index 8314a36..b078780 100644
--- a/device.mk
+++ b/device.mk
@@ -149,3 +149,10 @@ $(call inherit-product, vendor/google/grizzly/grizzly-vendor.mk)
 # Face unlock enrollment app's user types, from stock preinstalled-packages-tuscany.xml
 PRODUCT_COPY_FILES += \
     device/google/grizzly/configs/sysconfig/preinstalled-packages-faceenroll.xml:$(TARGET_COPY_OUT_SYSTEM_EXT)/etc/sysconfig/preinstalled-packages-faceenroll.xml
+
+# KernelSU Next manager, byte for byte as upstream signed it, with its arm64 libs
+# (vendor/extra/ksu, which ExpressiveOS's expressiveos-cheetah/ksu/apply-ksu.sh
+# stages). A normal, unprivileged app: no app gets root until the user grants it
+# there.
+PRODUCT_PACKAGES += \
+    KernelSUNext
diff --git a/ksu/config.fs b/ksu/config.fs
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..b0d8183
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ksu/config.fs
@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+# KernelSU Next manager (ExpressiveOS). Android never unpacks native libs for a
+# system app it hasn't updated, so the build installs the manager's libs in its
+# nativeLibraryDir, and the manager runs libksud.so from there as a program.
+# Files on /product are 0644 unless listed here.
+[product/app/KernelSUNext/lib/arm64/libksud.so]
+mode: 0755
+user: AID_ROOT
+group: AID_ROOT
+caps: 0
-- 
2.43.0

